---
schema_version: "1.0.0"
ticket_id: "OMN-19587"
title: "Autobind OCC evidence for OMN-19587"
summary: "OCC Evidence-Source autobind companion (OMN-13317 F1) for PR #2344."
is_seam_ticket: false
interface_change: false
interfaces_touched: []
requirements:
  - id: "req-transcribed-acceptance-criteria"
    statement: |-
      The acceptance criteria this ticket's author declared, transcribed from the ticket body at autobind time by occ-autobind. The ticket body is the source and this block is the copy; each criterion's id is the label the sibling binds_ac entry claims.
    acceptance:
      - id: "AC1"
        statement: |-
          AC1: GET REST calls under repos/OmniNode-ai/ and search, and GraphQL documents with no mutation operation, run with the token from the read-token command -- falsifier: uv run pytest tests/scripts/test_gh_read_routing.py -k read -q
      - id: "AC2"
        statement: |-
          AC2: every other call (pr merge, pr edit, pr create, pr comment, label changes, any non-GET api method, GraphQL mutations, auth and user endpoints) runs on the ambient operator credential unchanged -- falsifier: uv run pytest tests/scripts/test_gh_read_routing.py -k mutation -q
      - id: "AC3"
        statement: |-
          AC3: when the read-token command is unset or fails, the call runs on the operator credential and the usage log records identity operator-fallback with the reason -- falsifier: uv run pytest tests/scripts/test_gh_read_routing.py -k fallback -q
      - id: "AC4"
        statement: |-
          AC4: a cached read token is stored mode 0600, reused for at most 50 minutes and never written to the usage log -- falsifier: uv run pytest tests/scripts/test_gh_read_routing.py -k cache -q
      - id: "AC5"
        statement: |-
          AC5: over a 30-minute window with lanes running, the operator X-RateLimit-Used rises by no more than the mutation calls the usage log records plus the background rate read in the 10 minutes before install -- falsifier: header readings at both ends of the window beside gh_usage_report.py for that window
evidence_requirements:
  - kind: "ci"
    description: "PR #2344 product diff scope present"
    command: "gh pr view ${PR_NUMBER} --repo ${REPO} --json files"
  - kind: "tests"
    description: |-
      Behavior proof for PR #2344 on OmniNode-ai/omniclaude, derived from the PR's own diff: the test target(s) it adds or changes. Bound as dod_evidence item `dod-occ-diff-derived-behavior-proof`, executed at cwd `${OMNI_HOME}/omniclaude`.
    command: "uv run pytest tests/scripts/test_gh_read_routing.py -q"
emergency_bypass:
