      captured output: 1 there (0 on the dev branch, which still inherits stdout).
    source: "generated"
    checks:
      - check_type: "command"
        check_value: |-
          gh api -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github.raw' "repos/OmniNode-ai/omniclaude/contents/scripts/user-bin/gh_route.py?ref=6da445321fb5d6abedc606971f42ea3dbbd76892" | grep -c 'env=app_env, capture_output=True'
  - id: "dod-accept-2245z-19587-ac2-writes-on-operator"
    description: |-
      AC2 binding proposed by lane dod-closeout-bind-2026-10-06T2245Z-c0 and accepted by a different lane, dod-closeout-accept-2026-10-06T2245Z-c0, after an independent re-run at omniclaude origin/dev 12cdab834a5b (44 passed). Every listed non-read (pr merge, edit, create, comment, label, non-GET api, GraphQL mutation, viewer, auth, user) runs real gh with the operator token and never mints, at router and installed-shim level. Both test files are absent at the parents of the implementing merges (omniclaude#2344 a5432e08^, #2368 e988928b^).
    source: "manual"
    execution_scope: "local_done_gate"
    checks:
      - check_type: "test_passes"
        check_value: |-
          env -u PYTHONPATH uv run pytest "tests/scripts/test_gh_read_routing.py::test_mutation_and_non_read_run_on_operator_unchanged" "tests/scripts/test_gh_shim_read_routing.py::test_route_writes_never_routed_to_spy" -q -p no:cacheprovider
        cwd: "${OMNI_HOME}/omniclaude"
    binds_ac:
